 To achieve this cleanly, I used a Data-Attribute Override Architecture . 

 The app natively loads the CSS for Style 1 (Flat) . 

 When you hit the slider, JavaScript injects data-theme="clay" into the <body> tag. 

 This instantly activates a block of CSS overrides at the bottom of your stylesheet, morphing the variables, shadows, borders, and paddings into Style 2 (Claymorphism) without reloading the page. 

 Your preference is saved in LocalStorage, so it remembers your favorite theme the next day. 

