You've spotted a classic Streamlit challenge! The issue is with how state is being managed between the sidebar (where you select a trace) and the main content area (where the Trace ID is displayed in a text box). When you click the "Select this Trace" button, the app reruns, but the state updates aren't flowing cleanly to the main text input. 

 The problem is caused by using two different session state variables ( selected_trace_id_state and trace_id_input ) to manage the same piece of information, which leads to them getting out of sync. 

 Here is the corrected code. I've made the following key changes: 

 Simplified State Management : We will now use a single session state variable, st.session_state.trace_id_input , as the one source of truth for the selected Trace ID. 

 Used a Callback : The "Select this Trace" button now uses an on_click callback. This is a more reliable way to update the state in Streamlit. When the button is clicked, it calls a simple function to update st.session_state.trace_id_input directly. 

 Cleaned up Initialization : Removed the extra state variables and simplified the logic to ensure the text box in the main panel always reflects the correct selection from the sidebar. 

 This approach is more robust and solves the search functionality issue. 

