 Summary of Changes: 

 1. Font Updates for Softer Edges and Readability: 

 New Fonts: I've replaced Orbitron with Poppins for titles and headings, and Montserrat with Roboto for general body text. Both Poppins and Roboto are popular, modern fonts with softer, slightly rounded characteristics that are easier on the eyes.
 <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Roboto:wght@300;400;700&family=Poppins:wght@400;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">

 CSS Font-Family Updates: 

 body : font-family: 'Roboto', sans-serif; 

 .navbar-brand , .hero h1 , .logo-large , .section-title , .feature-title , .step-number , .cta-title : font-family: 'Poppins', sans-serif; 

 2. Neutral Colors for Text and Foreground: 

 New CSS Variables: I've introduced new CSS variables for text colors to provide more neutral options:

 --text-light: #f0f0f0; (A softer white for main text) 

 --text-medium: #c0c0c0; (A slightly darker gray for secondary text, links, and step descriptions) 

 --text-dark: #a0a0a0; (For less prominent text like the footer) 

 Application: These new variables have been applied to body text, nav-link color, hero p , .tagline , .section-title , .feature-card p , .step text, .step h3 , .step-number (to ensure visibility on gradient), and .footer . 

 Card Background and Border: The feature-card now uses --card-bg: rgba(26, 26, 74, 0.6); and --card-border: rgba(122, 0, 255, 0.3); for a slightly more opaque background and softer border, improving contrast with the neutral text. 

 Navbar Background: Increased opacity slightly for better visual separation: background: rgba(10, 10, 42, 0.6); 

 3. Feature Card Spacing and Future Scalability: 

 Bootstrap Grid Update: The id="features" section now uses Bootstrap's gutter classes ( g-4 ) and responsive column classes ( row-cols-1 row-cols-md-2 row-cols-lg-3 ) on the row element.
 <div class="row row-cols-1 row-cols-md-2 row-cols-lg-3 g-4">

 g-4 : Adds a default gap of 1.5rem (24px) between columns and rows, providing the desired spacing. 

 row-cols-* : Ensures that on small screens ( col-1 ), medium screens ( col-md-2 ), and large screens ( col-lg-3 ), the cards will arrange themselves in 1, 2, or 3 columns respectively, maintaining equal spacing and responsiveness. 

 Flexbox for Card Content: I've added display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: space-between; to .feature-card to ensure that content within each card (icon, title, paragraph) is consistently aligned, even if card content length varies. 

 Easy Expansion: With the row-cols-* and g-4 setup, you can simply add more <div class="col">...</div> elements within the row and they will automatically arrange themselves with the correct spacing and responsiveness. I've included an example "Coming Soon!" card to illustrate this. 

 4. 3D Elements Update: 

 As requested, I did not touch the overall background elements or the particle system. 

 I've changed the central "AI Core" from an IcosahedronGeometry (which looks like a complex sphere) to a TorusKnotGeometry in the Three.js script. This provides a different 3D shape (a knot-like torus) while retaining the wireframe, transparent, and animated properties you liked.
 const coreGeometry = new THREE.TorusKnotGeometry(1.5, 0.4, 100, 16); // Changed to TorusKnot
// ...
core.rotation.z = elapsedTime * 0.08; // Added Z rotation for TorusKnot

I've also added a small Z-axis rotation to the TorusKnot for more dynamic movement. 

 This updated design should offer a more visually appealing and user-friendly experience with improved aesthetics and maintainability. 

 Feel free to deploy this updated code or let me know if you'd like any further adjustments!

