 Key Changes Explained: 

 @font-face Rule (in <style> block): 

 @font-face {
 font-family: 'TapemFont'; /* This is the name you'll use in your CSS */
 src: url('assets/tapem.ttf') format('truetype'); /* Path to your font file */
 font-weight: normal;
 font-style: normal;
 font-display: swap; /* Improves performance by displaying text with a fallback font until the custom font is loaded */
}

 This is the CSS rule that tells the browser: "Hey, there's a custom font called TapemFont , and you can find its file at assets/tapem.ttf . It's a truetype font." 

 font-display: swap; is a good practice for performance. It tells the browser to display text using a generic fallback font immediately, and then swap to TapemFont once it's fully loaded. 

 Applying the Font to ASTRA Logos: 

 .navbar-brand :
 .navbar-brand {
 font-family: 'TapemFont', sans-serif; /* Applied custom font */
 font-weight: 700;
 font-size: 1.8rem;
 color: var(--neutral) !important;
 letter-spacing: 1.5px;
}

I've changed font-family: 'Poppins', sans-serif; to font-family: 'TapemFont', sans-serif; . This applies your custom font. sans-serif is a fallback in case the custom font fails to load. 

 .footer-logo :
 .footer-logo {
 font-family: 'TapemFont', sans-serif; /* Applied custom font */
 font-size: 2.5rem;
 font-weight: 700;
 margin-bottom: 20px;
 color: var(--neutral);
}

Similarly, the font-family here is updated to TapemFont . 

 Before You Deploy: 

 Ensure tapem.ttf is in assets/ : Double-check that your tapem.ttf file is correctly placed inside the assets folder. If it's in a subfolder (e.g., assets/fonts/tapem.ttf ), you'll need to adjust the src URL in the @font-face rule accordingly. 

 Font Compatibility: TrueType Font ( .ttf ) is widely supported across modern browsers, but for maximum compatibility across all browsers and devices, you might consider converting your font to other formats like .woff and .woff2 and including them in your src declaration within @font-face for better browser support and performance:
 @font-face {
 font-family: 'TapemFont';
 src: url('assets/tapem.woff2') format('woff2'),
 url('assets/tapem.woff') format('woff'),
 url('assets/tapem.ttf') format('truetype'); /* Keep .ttf as a fallback */
 font-weight: normal;
 font-style: normal;
 font-display: swap;
}

You can use online font converters (like Font Squirrel's Webfont Generator) to get these formats. 

 Now, your "ASTRA" headers will reflect your unique branding with the tapem.ttf font!

