 Why this changes the conversation with her: 

 Open the shop.html file in your browser, switch it to Mobile View (F12 -> Mobile Toggle). 

 Click "Build" on a custom cake. The bottom sheet slides up gracefully just like Swiggy. 

 The add-ons aren't just checkboxes; they have high-quality thumbnails with highlight borders when selected. 

 The UI is rendered dynamically from JavaScript arrays, proving to her that this isn't a static template, but a fully functional application layer.

This is exactly the kind of architectural maturity needed for serious agentic AI development. By shifting from a purely autonomous loop to a "Human-in-the-Loop as an Editor" model, you bypass the LLM's tendency to chase its own tail when debugging complex logic (like that lossy Base62 modulo operation). 

 It gives you the control of a traditional Python IDE while keeping the AI as your rapid-prototyping engine. 

 To build this, we are going to implement a split-pane layout. The left side remains the chat console, and the right side becomes a dedicated Manual Testing Sandbox . We will also add a dedicated FastAPI route to execute your sandbox code safely without polluting the LangGraph agent's memory stream. 

 Here is the complete implementation. 

 1. Backend Overhaul: app.py 

 We need to add a dedicated REST endpoint for your manual tests. This allows the UI to execute code directly on the server without going through the LangGraph WebSocket stream. 

 Add this code to your app.py (ensure you import BaseModel and traceback ): 

 import os, json, traceback
from fastapi import FastAPI, WebSocket, WebSocketDisconnect
from fastapi.responses import HTMLResponse
from pydantic import BaseModel
from dotenv import load_dotenv
from langchain_openai import ChatOpenAI
from langchain_core.messages import ToolMessage
from langgraph.checkpoint.memory import MemorySaver
from mcp import ClientSession
from mcp.client.sse import sse_client
from langchain_mcp_adapters.tools import load_mcp_tools
from main import build_agent, DANGEROUS_TOOLS

load_dotenv()
app = FastAPI()
memory = MemorySaver()

# --- NEW: Pydantic model for manual testing ---
class ManualTestPayload(BaseModel):
 name: str
 code: str
 test_payload: dict

# --- NEW: Dedicated manual test endpoint ---
@app.post("/api/test-manual")
async def run_manual_test(req: ManualTestPayload):
 """Executes code drafted in the UI Sandbox instantly."""
 indented_code = "\n".join([f" {line}" for line in req.code.split("\n")])
 wrapper = f"async def _run_sandbox(args):\n{indented_code}"
 namespace = {}
 try:
 exec(wrapper, globals(), namespace)
 result = await namespace['_run_sandbox'](req.test_payload)
 return {"status": "success", "result": result}
 except Exception as e:
 return {
 "status": "error", 
 "error_type": type(e).__name__, 
 "details": str(e),
 "traceback": traceback.format_exc()
 }

@app.get("/")
# ... (rest of your existing app.py code remains exactly the same) ...

