You are completely right. Streamlit was originally designed for data science dashboards, not asynchronous, multi-step AI agents. 

 The exact error you hit ( unhandled errors in a TaskGroup ) happens because Streamlit's synchronous loop loses track of LangGraph's background thread. When you typed "yes", Streamlit tried to start a brand new conversation instead of resuming the paused one, causing the server to crash. 

 Moving to a FastAPI Backend + HTML/JS Frontend via WebSockets is the professional, production-ready way to do this. It gives you a buttery-smooth chat UI and handles the "Pause/Resume" logic flawlessly. 

