 However, there is one small catch: standard HTML/CSS/JS files running inside a normal web browser (like Chrome or Safari) are trapped inside their browser tabs. A website cannot break out of Chrome to sit on top of your VS Code or WhatsApp. 

 To make your HTML/CSS/JS code run as a desktop app that can float on top of everything else, you just need a tiny wrapper. The most popular tool for this is Electron.js , which literally lets you build desktop apps using standard web technologies. (Fun fact: VS Code and Discord are actually built exactly this way!). 

 Here is how the architecture looks when you build it entirely with web tech: 

 How it works in plain HTML, CSS, and JS 

