 To fix the "boxy, sharpy" look while keeping the brilliant step-by-step functionality, we need to apply modern "Soft UI" principles. 

 Here is exactly how we transform that corporate grid into a luxury bakery experience: 

 Kill the Hard Angles: We replace all border-radius: 0 with border-radius: 24px (squircular shapes). 

 Ditch the Borders: Instead of harsh grey lines outlining every box, we use the background color of the page to separate elements, combined with very soft, large-spread drop shadows ( box-shadow: 0 10px 40px rgba(0,0,0,0.04) ). 

 Circular Toppings: Instead of putting toppings and accessories in rectangles, we put them in elegant circles or pill-shaped chips. It feels much more organic and appetizing. 

 The "Sticky Summary": Instead of making the user scroll up and down to remember what they picked, we lock a sleek order summary to the bottom or side of the screen. 

