 Here is a breakdown of how you can structure the game logic and bring the "Maa Hotel Delivery Speedrun" to life. 

 Game Design Breakdown 

 To make the game engaging and repeatable for that leaderboard, you need a balance of speed and obstacle management. 

 The Player: A pixel-art sprite of a "Legend" with long hair, riding a vintage sports bike (like an RX100 or a Hayabusa). 

 The Objective: Drive from the left side of the screen (Maa Hotel) to the right side (JSCA Stadium) before the timer runs out. 

 The Obstacles: * Traffic Police: Stand on the side of the road and try to flag you down.

 Ranchi Traffic: Randomly spawning autorickshaws, stray cows, and potholes. 

 The "Wide Call" Mechanic: Pressing the Spacebar triggers an animation where the Legend stretches his arms out.

 Effect: Grants a 1.5-second immunity window where traffic cops let you pass. 

 Cooldown: A 3-second cooldown prevents players from simply spamming the wide call the entire drive. 

 Tech Stack & Architecture 

 Keeping it lightweight is key to browser game success. 

 Component Technology Why it works here 
 Game Engine Phaser.js Perfect for 2D, 8-bit physics, and handles sprite animations effortlessly. 
 Frontend Vanilla JS or React Easy to wrap the Phaser canvas and build a simple UI for the start screen. 
 Leaderboard Supabase or Firebase Free-tier real-time databases that easily handle score fetching and posting. 
 Hosting Vercel Seamless CI/CD deployment straight from your GitHub repo. 

 Phaser.js Logic Concept (The Wide Call) 

 Here is a conceptual snippet of how you would handle the "Twist" mechanic in your Phaser update() loop. 

 // Inside your Phaser Scene class

update(time, delta) {
 // 1. Basic Bike Movement (Speeding up)
 if (this.cursors.right.isDown) {
 this.bike.setVelocityX(300); // Overspeeding!
 }

 // 2. The "Wide Call" Mechanic (Spacebar)
 if (Phaser.Input.Keyboard.JustDown(this.cursors.space) && !this.isCooldown) {
 this.triggerWideCall();
 }

 // 3. Traffic Police Collision Check
 this.physics.add.overlap(this.bike, this.cops, this.handleCopEncounter, null, this);
}

triggerWideCall() {
 this.isImmune = true;
 this.isCooldown = true;
 this.bike.play('wide_stretch_animation'); // Play the theatrical arm stretch

 // Immunity lasts for 1.5 seconds
 this.time.delayedCall(1500, () => {
 this.isImmune = false;
 this.bike.play('normal_riding_animation');
 });

 // Cooldown lasts for 3 seconds
 this.time.delayedCall(3000, () => {
 this.isCooldown = false;
 });
}

handleCopEncounter(bike, cop) {
 if (this.isImmune) {
 // The cop is stunned by the aura. Show a text popup!
 this.showPopupText("Thala for a reason!", cop.x, cop.y - 20);
 cop.disableBody(true, true); // Cop disappears or steps aside
 } else {
 // Player gets a challan. Game Over!
 this.gameOver("Challan Issued! Delivery Failed.");
 }
}

