 messageInput.value = "";
 loadingIndicator.style.display = "block"; // Show loading
 scrollToBottom();
 }

 function sendAction(actionType) {
 approvalBox.style.display = "none";
 chatBox.style.display = "flex";
 loadingIndicator.style.display = "block";

 ws.send(JSON.stringify({ action: actionType }));
 }

 function handleKeyPress(event) {
 if (event.key === "Enter") sendMessage();
 }

 function scrollToBottom() {
 chatContainer.scrollTo({ top: chatContainer.scrollHeight, behavior: 'smooth' });
 }
 </script>
</body>
</html>

 What you will notice immediately: 

 No More Text Walls: When it generates that massive Base62 script, it now says "🛠️ Preparing Tool Execution: build_custom_tool " with a small, golden "View Execution Payload" dropdown. It keeps your chat history immaculately clean. 

 Clear Feedback: When you ask it a question, a pulsing "Agent is thinking..." indicator shows up so you know it's working. 

 No More Generic Pauses: When it stops, the UI will specifically flash: "⚠️ Approval Required: build_custom_tool " . You know exactly what button you are clicking. 

 Restart your FastAPI server ( uv run uvicorn app:app --port 8001 ) and refresh your browser. How does the interface feel now?

This is a fantastic direction. Moving the toggle to the header cleans up the layout, and shifting the Claymorphism theme to a Light Mode / White Clay (often called Neumorphism) creates a stunning, high-contrast dynamic when switching from the flat dark mode. 

 Here is the complete, updated index.html . 

 What changed: 

 Header UI: The toggle is now seamlessly integrated into the top right header buttons. The text labels are gone, leaving a clean, pill-shaped slider. 

 Light Clay Theme: I completely rewrote the [data-theme="clay"] variables. It now uses a crisp off-white/cool-gray palette ( #e0e5ec ). The box shadows use a white top-left highlight and a cool-gray bottom-right shadow to create that perfect, soft, 3D extruded clay look. 

 Smart Color Overrides: Dark mode uses white text ( .text-white ), but when you toggle to Light Clay, the CSS automatically forces all those text elements to flip to a deep slate gray ( #2d3436 ) so everything is perfectly readable. 

