 The Skeuomorphic Upgrades Explained: 

 The Set Bubbles (Hardware Buttons): Notice they no longer display numbers by default. They look like blank rubber pads. When you tap them, the shadow inverts ( inset ), the border disappears, and the var(--led-green) glows, making it feel exactly like turning on a piece of electronic equipment. 

 LCD Screens ( .lcd-badge ): The Rep/Set counters and the Date display now use a recessed digital screen aesthetic with monospace fonts and a glowing yellow text-shadow . 

 The Finisher Toggle: Instead of a standard checkbox, I built a pure CSS mechanical toggle switch. When turned on, the inside of the track glows red, and the raised physical nub slides over and casts its own drop shadow. 

 The Progress Groove: The background track ( .progress ) uses deep inner shadows to look like a trench routed into the metal background. The progress-bar uses an outer glow to look like liquid neon filling the trench. 

 Deploy this, open it on your phone, and tap one of the set bubbles. The tactile visual feedback is next level!

This is an incredibly fun direction. Skeuomorphism—designing UI elements to look and feel like physical, real-world objects—is making a massive comeback (often called "Neumorphism" or modern Skeuomorphism). 

 To achieve this for FitForge, we need to move away from "flat" colors and introduce textures, bevels, lighting, and physical shadows . 

 Here is what I have transformed in the CSS: 

 The Gym Mat Background: The background is no longer a flat dark color. It now has a subtle, perforated rubber texture, simulating the floor of a premium gym. 

 Heavy-Duty Equipment Cards: The workout cards now look like molded metallic/plastic plates with beveled edges, engraved text effects, and deep drop shadows. 

 Tactile Push-Buttons (The Sets): This is the best part. The set bubbles now look like physical rubberized buttons. When you tap them, they physically depress into the screen ( transform: translateY(4px) ) and illuminate from the inside with a neon green LED glow. 

 The Marquee Display: The animated "FITFORGE" text you requested is now housed inside an inset, glass-like digital display screen. 

 The Stopwatch: The floating timer has been redesigned to look like a heavy, rugged tactical stopwatch with a recessed LCD screen for the countdown. 

 Here is your complete, fully skeuomorphic index.html . 

