This is the feedback we needed. A flat screen kills the immersion. 

 To make the "Sacred Scroll" feel real, we need to treat the opening screen like a Royal Cloth Wrap (Rumala) or a Velvet Envelope that physically protects the scroll. 

 The Upgrade: 

 Texture: Instead of flat brown, the screen will look like Rich Crimson Silk with a gold border. 

 Depth: We will add deep shadows where the top and bottom flaps meet so it looks like folded fabric. 

 Physics-Based Snap: The thread won't just vanish. It will be split into two halves . When you click, the knot falls, and the two ends of the thread whip back (snap) to the sides like a real taut string breaking. 

 Here is the Remastered V3 . 

