This is a significant architectural upgrade. You are moving from a monolithic app (Streamlit does everything) to a Microservices Architecture . 

 Service 1: Agent Chat (Streamlit, Port 8501) - The Logic. 

 Service 2: Saksh Dashboard (FastAPI + HTML/JS, Port 2604) - The Monitor. 

 Here is the complete implementation. 

 1. The Project Structure 

 📂 project_root/
 ├── 📂 agents/ # (Same as before)
 ├── 📂 templates/ # NEW: HTML files
 │ └── index.html 
 ├── saksh.py # (Core Engine - No change)
 ├── adapters.py # (Connectors - No change)
 ├── saksh_api.py # NEW: The Dashboard Server
 └── app.py # (Streamlit Chat - Minimized)

 2. The Dashboard Server ( saksh_api.py ) 

 This replaces the sidebar. It uses FastAPI to serve your HTML and raw JSON data on Port 2604. 

 import uvicorn
from fastapi import FastAPI, Request
from fastapi.responses import HTMLResponse
from fastapi.templating import Jinja2Templates
from fastapi.staticfiles import StaticFiles

# Import Saksh Core
from saksh import Saksh
from adapters import CrewAINetra
from agents.qwen_agent import get_qwen_agent
from agents.gpt_agent import get_gpt_agent

# 1. Initialize App & Templates
app = FastAPI()
templates = Jinja2Templates(directory="templates")

# 2. Initialize Saksh System (The Independent Monitor)
# We recreate the agent objects here just to get their configs/keys.
# This confirms the monitor is truly separate from the chat app.
observer = Saksh()

print("👁️ SAKSH: Initializing Surveillance Systems...")
qwen = get_qwen_agent()
gpt = get_gpt_agent()

# Register Eyes
observer.open_eye(CrewAINetra(qwen, "Qwen-Custom-Server"))
observer.open_eye(CrewAINetra(gpt, "OpenAI-GPT4-Core"))

# 3. API Routes

@app.get("/", response_class=HTMLResponse)
async def read_dashboard(request: Request):
 """Serves the actual HTML Dashboard"""
 return templates.TemplateResponse("index.html", {"request": request})

@app.get("/api/health")
async def get_health_metrics():
 """The endpoint your JS will poll every 2 seconds"""
 return observer.observe()

# 4. Entry Point
if __name__ == "__main__":
 print("🚀 Saksh Dashboard running at http://localhost:2604")
 uvicorn.run(app, host="0.0.0.0", port=2604)

 3. The Frontend ( templates/index.html ) 

 This is a professional, dark-themed dashboard using Bootstrap 5 and jQuery . No Python logic here—pure web tech. 

