Of course! I've updated the CSS to stylize the sidebar's scrollbar using your theme's root colors and to make it discreetly hide when it's not being used. 

 The scrollbar will now be thin and rounded, using your primary brand color. It will only become fully visible when you hover your mouse over the sidebar area, providing a cleaner look. 

 Here is the complete index.html file with the new scrollbar styles. 

 <!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
 <meta charset="UTF-8"/>
 <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0"/>
 <title>Agentarium</title>
 <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Material+Symbols+Outlined:opsz,wght,FILL,GRAD@20..48,100..700,0..1,-50..200" />
 <link href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.3.0/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css" rel="stylesheet"/>
 <link href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/vis-network@9.1.2/dist/vis-network.min.css" rel="stylesheet"/>
 <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap-icons@1.11.3/font/bootstrap-icons.min.css">
 <style>
 @import url('https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Tourney:ital,wght@0,100..900;1,100..900&display=swap');
 </style>
 <style>
 :root{
 --brand-primary:#6c4df6; --brand-primary-600:#5a3ef0; --brand-primary-700:#4a32e3;
 --brand-accent:#22c55e; --brand-accent-600:#16a34a;
 --ink-900:#0f172a; --ink-700:#334155; --ink-500:#64748b;
 --surface:#ffffff; --border:#e5e7eb;
 }
 html, body {
 height: 100vh;
 overflow: hidden;
 }
 body{ background:linear-gradient(180deg,#f3f5ff 0%, #f9fafb 30%, #f7f8ff 100%); color:var(--ink-900); }
 .page-wrapper {
 height: 100%;
 display: flex;
 flex-direction: column;
 }
 .main-content-row {
 flex-grow: 1;
