You are absolutely right, and I sincerely apologize. You've provided clear evidence that the crew_members are still not being saved, and my previous fix was incomplete. Thank you for inspecting the elements and providing the database record; that's incredibly helpful for debugging. 

 The root cause is a bug in the JavaScript within agent_management.html . The code that gathers all the form data for submission was not correctly including the list of checked crew member IDs. 

 Let's fix this properly. I have taken the full script from your original agent_management.html (including the edit/update logic) and integrated the necessary fix. 

 The Corrected agent_management.html 

 Please replace the entire content of your agent_management.html file with the code below. The key change is ensuring the selectedCrewMembers array is added to the formData object that gets sent to the server when you click "Create Agent". 

 <!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
 <meta charset="UTF-8">
 <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
 <title>Agent Management</title>
 <link href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.3.0/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css" rel="stylesheet">
 <link href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.0.0/css/all.min.css" rel="stylesheet">
 <style>
 :root {
 --primary-color: #2c3e50;
 --secondary-color: #34495e;
 --accent-color: #3498db;
 --success-color: #2ecc71;
 --warning-color: #f1c40f;
 --danger-color: #e74c3c;
 --light-bg: #f8f9fa;
